{
    "algorithm": "The X-Byomailer-Signature header is \"sha256=\" and the lowercase hex HMAC-SHA256 of the signed payload. The signed payload is the X-Byomailer-Timestamp value, a dot and the raw request body. The key is the full endpoint secret, with its \"whsec_\" prefix. Trim the received header value, change it to lowercase and compare it in constant time. Reject a timestamp that is more than tolerance_seconds before or after now.",
    "checks": "Do the checks in this order. The first check that fails gives the reason. 1: the signature header is present (signature). 2: the timestamp header is present and has only digits (timestamp). 3: the signature matches (signature). 4: the timestamp is inside the tolerance (timestamp). 5: the body is a JSON object (payload).",
    "fields": "A null signature or timestamp means that the header is missing. delivery is the X-Byomailer-Delivery header, or null when the header is missing. delivery_id is the delivery ID that a valid case must return.",
    "headers": {
        "signature": "X-Byomailer-Signature",
        "timestamp": "X-Byomailer-Timestamp",
        "event": "X-Byomailer-Event",
        "delivery": "X-Byomailer-Delivery"
    },
    "tolerance_seconds": 300,
